{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba census-result.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# The census of link decisions over the window: gate PASS by the registered rule; direction unsettled (D700, D701; 2026-11-21)\n     2\t\n     3\tRun: `poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/` (three draws, each counted: complete, both July seq-148 answers reused, equal to old-2 with no\n     4\tlink row; one ledger at Alex's $0.10: settled $0.0266 at the ledger's rule of three times each reported input, 52 attempts, nothing\n     5\trefused or overrun). Scored by `read_census.py` against `expected-links.json` (written before any census answer; R 1, W 38, O 66):\n     6\t`census-result.md`.\n     7\t\n     8\t## By the registered rule\n     9\t- **Known positive (v9 Data Center FY2027 reads v14 total revenue FY2027, together):** right in 3 of 3 draws; margins 0.05, 0.09,\n    10\t  0.03 (the July samples, fragile).\n    11\t- **W pairs (38, the shown material names no connection):** no link in any draw. Wrong links: 0.\n    12\t- **Gate: PASS.**\n    13\t\n    14\t## The O pairs that were linked (reported, not scored)\n    15\t\n    16\t| seq | pair | draw 1 | draw 2 | draw 3 | reading |\n    17\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n    18\t| 8 | v2 (all credit support, guarantees, backstops) – v1 (AI-cloud credit support) | v2 reads v1, 0.58 | v2 reads v1, 0.51 | no link (0.48) | a whole reads its part; 2 of 3 |\n    19\t| 265 | v16 (total CPU FY2027) – v14 (total revenue FY2027) | v16 reads v14, 0.82 | 0.82 | 0.83 | a part reads its whole; stable |\n    20\t| 321 | v17 (total revenue growth FY2028) – v16 (total CPU FY2027) | v17 reads v16, 0.50 | 0.50 | 0.55 | a company-wide figure reads a part of the year before; at the line |\n    21\t| 534 | v21 (total revenue growth FY2027) – v16 (total CPU FY2027) | v21 reads v16, 0.73 | 0.72 | 0.76 | a whole reads its part; stable |\n    22\t| 534 | v21 – v9 (Data Center FY2027) | v21 reads v9, 0.53 | **v9 reads v21**, 0.52 | v21 reads v9, 0.60 | the direction flips between draws |\n    23\t| 1238 | v35 (total revenue FY2028) – v14 (total revenue FY2027) | v35 reads v14, 0.52 | 0.54 | no link (0.44) | another period of the same quantity; 2 of 3 |\n    24\t| 1238 | v35 – v9 | no link | v35 reads v9, 0.50 | no link | 1 of 3 |\n    25\t\n    26\tEvery link written carried the sign together. Links per draw: 7, 8, 5.\n    27\t\n    28\t## What it shows\n    29\t- **No link between unrelated questions.** Across 3 × 38 W decisions, Jev never linked a financing amount to a revenue or margin\n    30\t  question, or two financing amounts of different kinds.\n    31\t- **The direction of a part against its whole is not settled by the criterion.** The same version reads part-to-whole (v9 → v14,\n    32\t  v16 → v14) and whole-to-part (v2 → v1, v21 → v16, v21 → v9), and one pair flips between draws (v21–v9). This is the class §3 named\n    33\t  (\"abstract\": the criterion's two clauses admit both directions), now counted on the whole window: of the 8 pairs linked in some draw,\n    34\t  4 take the same direction in 3 of 3 draws (v9 → v14, v16 → v14, v17 → v16, v21 → v16), 3 are linked in only 1 or 2 draws, and 1\n    35\t  flips direction.\n    36\t- **Fragile decisions:** 6 of the linked or required decisions sit within 0.10 of the next class (v9 → v14 in all three; v17 → v16 in\n    37\t  two; v21–v9 in one).\n    38\t\n    39\t## What it means for the paid run\n    40\t- A linked sequence of the paid run can take its link answers from its paired census draw: a link request depends on the candidate's\n    41\t  state and the shown question's card, ladder and first two evidence pieces, none of which a written link changes, so the requests are\n    42\t  the same (a circle correction, if any, would be new). The readers are then known before anything is bought: draw 1 and draw 2, v2,\n    43\t  v9, v16, v17, v21, v35; draw 3, v9, v16, v17, v21. Each control can retire exactly its paired draw's readers from each reader's first\n    44\t  link.\n    45\t- Priced from old-2's stored judgements at published rates: the readers' judgements from their links on cost about $1.0 per sequence\n    46\t  (v2 $0.26, v9 $0.30, v16 $0.15, v17 $0.15, v21 $0.13, v35 $0.05), plus the extra days a changed read question queues its reader\n    47\t  (estimate +30%); three linked and three controls about $7. An estimate, not a ceiling.\n    48\t- **The open question before buying judgements** (for the council, then Alex): measure the current wording as it is, with its\n    49\t  whole-to-part links and one flipping pair disclosed, or first settle the direction of a part against its whole in the criterion,\n    50\t  which changes what the system does (a new arm, probed on these 105 pairs at cents, then Alex).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/links.py | sed -n '17,68p;139,320p'\"","aggregated_output":"    17\tTHRESHOLD = jev_matching.THRESHOLD\n    18\tLABELS = vocabulary.ASSET_LABELS                 # five-rung asset ladders run Strongly bullish .. Strongly bearish, or the reverse\n    19\tCANDIDATE_READS, THESIS_READS, NEITHER = 'candidate_reads_thesis', 'thesis_reads_candidate', 'neither'\n    20\tTOGETHER, OPPOSITE, NO_SIGN = 'together', 'opposite', 'no_clear_sign'\n    21\t\n    22\tREADS = {\n    23\t    CANDIDATE_READS: \"the CANDIDATE should be judged with the THESIS's current conclusion in view, because the THESIS's answer bounds \"\n    24\t                     \"or drives the CANDIDATE's: a part read against its whole (one product line's sales against the company's total \"\n    25\t                     \"sales; one region's loan book against the bank's total loans), or a quantity read against another it depends on \"\n    26\t                     \"(a component supplier's revenue against its largest customer's capital spending; an airline's fuel bill against \"\n    27\t                     \"its fuel volume)\",\n    28\t    THESIS_READS: \"the THESIS should be judged with the CANDIDATE's current conclusion in view, for the same reasons with the roles swapped\",\n    29\t    NEITHER: \"neither answer bounds or drives the other: unrelated quantities (a retailer's gross margin and its store openings in \"\n    30\t             \"another country), or the same quantity for the same period and scope; sharing a company, industry or topic is not enough\",\n    31\t}\n    32\tSIGN = {\n    33\t    TOGETHER: \"a higher answer to the question read makes a higher answer to the question reading it more likely (a company's total \"\n    34\t              \"sales and one product line's sales, when that line's share of the total holds steady; a customer's capital spending \"\n    35\t              \"and its component supplier's revenue)\",\n    36\t    OPPOSITE: \"a higher answer to the question read makes a lower answer to the question reading it more likely (an airline's fuel \"\n    37\t              \"bill and its operating margin; a retailer's markdowns and its gross margin)\",\n    38\t    NO_SIGN: \"the question read only caps the other without moving its most likely answer (a regulator's cap on a bank's fees set far \"\n    39\t             \"above what it charges), or the supplied text does not show which way it moves it\",\n    40\t}\n    41\tREADS_INSTRUCTIONS = (\"Should one of these two questions be judged with the other's current conclusion in view? Use only the supplied \"\n    42\t                      \"text. THESIS:\\n\")\n    43\tSIGN_INSTRUCTIONS = {\n    44\t    CANDIDATE_READS: \"If the THESIS's answer turned out higher, which way would that move the CANDIDATE's most likely answer? Use only the supplied text. THESIS:\\n\",\n    45\t    THESIS_READS: \"If the CANDIDATE's answer turned out higher, which way would that move the THESIS's most likely answer? Use only the supplied text. THESIS:\\n\",\n    46\t}\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\tclass Refused(RuntimeError):\n    50\t    \"\"\"The link step cannot finish for this article (a persistent circle, an unbound waiting row, a Jev failure); `record` says why.\"\"\"\n    51\t\n    52\t    def __init__(self, message, record):\n    53\t        super().__init__(message)\n    54\t        self.record = record\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\tdef reads_question(text, excluded=None, note=''):\n    58\t    criteria = {k: v for k, v in READS.items() if k != excluded}\n    59\t    return {'type': 'choice', 'criteria': criteria, 'instructions': READS_INSTRUCTIONS.replace('THESIS:\\n', (note + ' ' if note else '') + 'THESIS:\\n') + text}\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\tdef sign_question(text, direction):\n    63\t    return {'type': 'choice', 'criteria': dict(SIGN), 'instructions': SIGN_INSTRUCTIONS[direction] + text}\n    64\t\n    65\t\n    66\t# ---------- identity: which ladders are number ladders, and the label ----------\n    67\t\n    68\tdef typed_direction(rungs):\n   139\t# ---------- the reading graph ----------\n   140\t\n   141\tdef stored_edges(conn):\n   142\t    \"\"\"Every stored dependency at its effective target (a bound wait counts through the question it is bound to).\"\"\"\n   143\t    edges = {}\n   144\t    for (view_id,) in conn.execute('select distinct view_id from dependencies'):\n   145\t        for dep in store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id):\n   146\t            if dep['resolved_to']:\n   147\t                edges.setdefault(view_id, set()).add(dep['resolved_to'])\n   148\t    return edges\n   149\t\n   150\t\n   151\tdef unbound_waits(conn):\n   152\t    return conn.execute(\"select count(*) from dependencies where coalesce(depends_on, '')='' and coalesce(wait_year, '')!='' \"\n   153\t                        \"and dependency_id not in (select dependency_id from dependency_resolutions)\").fetchone()[0]\n   154\t\n   155\t\n   156\tdef circles(conn, proposed):\n   157\t    \"\"\"The proposed links (reader, read) that lie on a circle of the stored relation plus every proposed link, each with one path.\"\"\"\n   158\t    graph = {k: set(v) for k, v in stored_edges(conn).items()}\n   159\t    for link in proposed:\n   160\t        graph.setdefault(link['reader'], set()).add(link['read'])\n   161\t    found = []\n   162\t    for link in proposed:\n   163\t        stack, seen = [(link['read'], [link['reader'], link['read']])], set()\n   164\t        while stack:\n   165\t            node, path = stack.pop()\n   166\t            if node == link['reader']:\n   167\t                found.append((link, path))\n   168\t                break\n   169\t            if node in seen:\n   170\t                continue\n   171\t            seen.add(node)\n   172\t            stack.extend((nxt, path + [nxt]) for nxt in sorted(graph.get(node, ())))\n   173\t    return found\n   174\t\n   175\t\n   176\t# ---------- selection ----------\n   177\t\n   178\tdef _ask(archive, cfg, jobs, transport, record, stage):\n   179\t    \"\"\"One Jev request per job, asked in order; each job is written into the record before it is sent (its request sha, whether the\n   180\t    archive held it) and completed as it is answered (its call id). A failure names the failing job's sha and leaves the later jobs\n   181\t    marked not asked.\"\"\"\n   182\t    entries = []\n   183\t    for state, questions in jobs:\n   184\t        _, sha = model.request_identity(jev.request_for(cfg.matching, state, questions))\n   185\t        entries.append({'stage': stage, 'request_sha256': sha, 'questions': sorted(questions), 'archived_before': bool(archive.lookup(sha)),\n   186\t                        'status': 'not asked'})\n   187\t    record['calls'].extend(entries)\n   188\t    replies = []\n   189\t    for entry, (state, questions) in zip(entries, jobs):\n   190\t        try:\n   191\t            reply = jev.ask(archive, cfg, cfg.matching, state, questions, 'match', transport=transport)\n   192\t        except Exception as error:\n   193\t            entry['status'] = 'failed'\n   194\t            record['error'] = f'{type(error).__name__}: {error}'[:300]\n   195\t            record['failed_request_sha256'] = entry['request_sha256']\n   196\t            raise Refused(f'link question failed: {record[\"error\"]}', record) from error\n   197\t        entry['status'], entry['call_id'] = 'answered', reply.call_id\n   198\t        replies.append(reply.data)\n   199\t    return replies\n   200\t\n   201\t\n   202\tdef _passes(answer, accepted):\n   203\t    choice = answer['choice']\n   204\t    return choice if choice in accepted and answer['probabilities'][choice] >= THRESHOLD else None\n   205\t\n   206\t\n   207\tdef choose(archive, cfg, conn, handover, checked, lists, shown_views, *, transport=None):\n   208\t    \"\"\"The links this article proposes: [{'reader', 'read', 'candidate', 'direction', 'sign'}], reader and read being a candidate id\n   209\t    (canonical) or a stored view id; and the record of how they were chosen. Raises Refused for an unbound waiting row, a Jev\n   210\t    failure or a circle that remains after one correction (PRD 06).\"\"\"\n   211\t    record = {'pairs': [], 'calls': [], 'corrections': [], 'proposed': []}\n   212\t    if unbound_waits(conn):\n   213\t        record['error'] = 'the store holds an unbound waiting dependency row'\n   214\t        raise Refused(record['error'], record)\n   215\t    aliases, problems = identity.batch_plan(handover.candidates, checked.outcomes)\n   216\t    if problems:                                   # the writer refuses the same plan (WriteConflict); nothing to ask\n   217\t        record['skipped'] = problems\n   218\t        return [], record\n   219\t    evidence = handover.evidence\n   220\t    stage1, asked = [], []\n   221\t    for c in handover.candidates:\n   222\t        outcome, target, _ = checked.outcomes.get(c['id'], ('skip', None, []))\n   223\t        if outcome not in ('new', 'succession') or aliases.get(c['id']) != c['id']:\n   224\t            continue\n   225\t        rungs = candidate_rungs(conn, c, outcome, target)\n   226\t        if not is_number_question(c['kind'], rungs, c.get('measure')):\n   227\t            record['pairs'].append({'candidate': c['id'], 'eligible': False, 'why': 'not a number question'})\n   228\t            continue\n   229\t        listed = list(dict.fromkeys(list(lists.candidate_lists.get(c['id'], [])) + [v['view_id'] for v in shown_views]))\n   230\t        theses = []\n   231\t        for view_id in listed:\n   232\t            ok = store.is_open(conn, view_id) and stored_is_number_question(conn, view_id)\n   233\t            record['pairs'].append({'candidate': c['id'], 'thesis': view_id, 'eligible': ok})\n   234\t            if ok:\n   235\t                theses.append(view_id)\n   236\t        if theses:\n   237\t            state = jev_matching.candidate_state(c, evidence)\n   238\t            stage1.append((state, {f'reads__{v}': reads_question(jev_matching.thesis_text(conn, v)) for v in theses}))\n   239\t            asked.append((c, state, theses))\n   240\t    if not stage1:\n   241\t        return [], record\n   242\t    answers = _ask(archive, cfg, stage1, transport, record, 'reads')\n   243\t    directions = {}\n   244\t    for (c, state, theses), reply in zip(asked, answers):\n   245\t        for view_id in theses:\n   246\t            answer = reply[f'reads__{view_id}']\n   247\t            direction = _passes(answer, (CANDIDATE_READS, THESIS_READS))\n   248\t            record['pairs'].append({'candidate': c['id'], 'thesis': view_id, 'reads': answer['choice'], 'probabilities': answer['probabilities']})\n   249\t            if direction:\n   250\t                directions[(c['id'], view_id)] = direction\n   251\t    links = _signed(archive, cfg, conn, asked, directions, transport, record)\n   252\t    on_circle = circles(conn, links)\n   253\t    if on_circle:\n   254\t        links = _corrected(archive, cfg, conn, asked, directions, links, on_circle, transport, record)\n   255\t        remaining = circles(conn, links)\n   256\t        if remaining:\n   257\t            record['error'] = 'persistent cycle: ' + '; '.join(' -> '.join(path) for _, path in remaining)\n   258\t            raise Refused(record['error'], record)\n   259\t    record['proposed'] = links\n   260\t    return links, record\n   261\t\n   262\t\n   263\tdef _signed(archive, cfg, conn, asked, directions, transport, record, stage='sign'):\n   264\t    jobs, owners = [], []\n   265\t    for c, state, theses in asked:\n   266\t        questions = {f'sign__{v}': sign_question(jev_matching.thesis_text(conn, v), directions[(c['id'], v)]) for v in theses if (c['id'], v) in directions}\n   267\t        if questions:\n   268\t            jobs.append((state, questions))\n   269\t            owners.append(c)\n   270\t    links = []\n   271\t    if not jobs:\n   272\t        return links\n   273\t    for c, reply in zip(owners, _ask(archive, cfg, jobs, transport, record, stage)):\n   274\t        for qid, answer in sorted(reply.items()):\n   275\t            view_id = qid[len('sign__'):]\n   276\t            sign = _passes(answer, (TOGETHER, OPPOSITE))\n   277\t            record['pairs'].append({'candidate': c['id'], 'thesis': view_id, 'sign': answer['choice'], 'probabilities': answer['probabilities']})\n   278\t            if sign:\n   279\t                direction = directions[(c['id'], view_id)]\n   280\t                reader, read = (c['id'], view_id) if direction == CANDIDATE_READS else (view_id, c['id'])\n   281\t                links.append({'reader': reader, 'read': read, 'candidate': c['id'], 'thesis': view_id, 'direction': direction, 'sign': sign})\n   282\t    return links\n   283\t\n   284\t\n   285\tdef _corrected(archive, cfg, conn, asked, directions, links, on_circle, transport, record):\n   286\t    \"\"\"PRD 06: refuse a circle and ask the model to correct it, once: the pair's READS question again, the offending direction removed\n   287\t    and the circle named; the answer replaces the original.\"\"\"\n   288\t    offending = {(link['candidate'], link['thesis']): path for link, path in on_circle}\n   289\t    jobs, owners = [], []\n   290\t    for c, state, theses in asked:\n   291\t        questions = {}\n   292\t        for view_id in theses:\n   293\t            path = offending.get((c['id'], view_id))\n   294\t            if path is None:\n   295\t                continue\n   296\t            excluded = directions[(c['id'], view_id)]\n   297\t            named = [('the CANDIDATE' if node == c['id'] else 'the THESIS' if node == view_id else node) for node in path]\n   298\t            note = f'Reading this way would make {named[0]} read itself through {\" -> \".join(named)}; a question cannot read its own conclusion.'\n   299\t            questions[f'reads__{view_id}'] = reads_question(jev_matching.thesis_text(conn, view_id), excluded=excluded, note=note)\n   300\t            record['corrections'].append({'candidate': c['id'], 'thesis': view_id, 'rejected': excluded, 'path': path})\n   301\t        if questions:\n   302\t            jobs.append((state, questions))\n   303\t            owners.append(c)\n   304\t    kept = [link for link in links if (link['candidate'], link['thesis']) not in offending]\n   305\t    corrected = {}\n   306\t    for c, reply in zip(owners, _ask(archive, cfg, jobs, transport, record, 'correction')):\n   307\t        for qid, answer in reply.items():\n   308\t            view_id = qid[len('reads__'):]\n   309\t            directions.pop((c['id'], view_id), None)\n   310\t            direction = _passes(answer, (CANDIDATE_READS, THESIS_READS))\n   311\t            record['corrections'].append({'candidate': c['id'], 'thesis': view_id, 'answer': answer['choice'], 'probabilities': answer['probabilities']})\n   312\t            if direction:\n   313\t                corrected[(c['id'], view_id)] = direction\n   314\t    if corrected:\n   315\t        directions.update(corrected)\n   316\t        regrouped = [(c, state, [v for v in theses if (c['id'], v) in corrected]) for c, state, theses in asked]\n   317\t        kept += _signed(archive, cfg, conn, [g for g in regrouped if g[2]], corrected, transport, record, stage='correction sign')\n   318\t    return kept\n   319\t\n   320\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba CENSUS-RESULT.md; nl -ba claude-r17.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# The census of link decisions over the window: gate PASS by the registered rule; direction unsettled (D700, D701; 2026-11-21)\n     2\t\n     3\tRun: `poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/` (three draws, each counted: complete, both July seq-148 answers reused, equal to old-2 with no\n     4\tlink row; one ledger at Alex's $0.10: settled $0.0266 at the ledger's rule of three times each reported input, 52 attempts, nothing\n     5\trefused or overrun). Scored by `read_census.py` against `expected-links.json` (written before any census answer; R 1, W 38, O 66):\n     6\t`census-result.md`.\n     7\t\n     8\t## By the registered rule\n     9\t- **Known positive (v9 Data Center FY2027 reads v14 total revenue FY2027, together):** right in 3 of 3 draws; margins 0.05, 0.09,\n    10\t  0.03 (the July samples, fragile).\n    11\t- **W pairs (38, the shown material names no connection):** no link in any draw. Wrong links: 0.\n    12\t- **Gate: PASS.**\n    13\t\n    14\t## The O pairs that were linked (reported, not scored)\n    15\t\n    16\t| seq | pair | draw 1 | draw 2 | draw 3 | reading |\n    17\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n    18\t| 8 | v2 (all credit support, guarantees, backstops) – v1 (AI-cloud credit support) | v2 reads v1, 0.58 | v2 reads v1, 0.51 | no link (0.48) | a whole reads its part; 2 of 3 |\n    19\t| 265 | v16 (total CPU FY2027) – v14 (total revenue FY2027) | v16 reads v14, 0.82 | 0.82 | 0.83 | a part reads its whole; stable |\n    20\t| 321 | v17 (total revenue growth FY2028) – v16 (total CPU FY2027) | v17 reads v16, 0.50 | 0.50 | 0.55 | a company-wide figure reads a part of the year before; at the line |\n    21\t| 534 | v21 (total revenue growth FY2027) – v16 (total CPU FY2027) | v21 reads v16, 0.73 | 0.72 | 0.76 | a whole reads its part; stable |\n    22\t| 534 | v21 – v9 (Data Center FY2027) | v21 reads v9, 0.53 | **v9 reads v21**, 0.52 | v21 reads v9, 0.60 | the direction flips between draws |\n    23\t| 1238 | v35 (total revenue FY2028) – v14 (total revenue FY2027) | v35 reads v14, 0.52 | 0.54 | no link (0.44) | another period of the same quantity; 2 of 3 |\n    24\t| 1238 | v35 – v9 | no link | v35 reads v9, 0.50 | no link | 1 of 3 |\n    25\t\n    26\tEvery link written carried the sign together. Links per draw: 7, 8, 5.\n    27\t\n    28\t## What it shows\n    29\t- **No link between unrelated questions.** Across 3 × 38 W decisions, Jev never linked a financing amount to a revenue or margin\n    30\t  question, or two financing amounts of different kinds.\n    31\t- **The direction of a part against its whole is not settled by the criterion.** The same version reads part-to-whole (v9 → v14,\n    32\t  v16 → v14) and whole-to-part (v2 → v1, v21 → v16, v21 → v9), and one pair flips between draws (v21–v9). This is the class §3 named\n    33\t  (\"abstract\": the criterion's two clauses admit both directions), now counted on the whole window: of the 8 pairs linked in some draw,\n    34\t  4 take the same direction in 3 of 3 draws (v9 → v14, v16 → v14, v17 → v16, v21 → v16), 3 are linked in only 1 or 2 draws, and 1\n    35\t  flips direction.\n    36\t- **Fragile decisions:** 6 of the linked or required decisions sit within 0.10 of the next class (v9 → v14 in all three; v17 → v16 in\n    37\t  two; v21–v9 in one).\n    38\t\n    39\t## What it means for the paid run\n    40\t- A linked sequence of the paid run can take its link answers from its paired census draw: a link request depends on the candidate's\n    41\t  state and the shown question's card, ladder and first two evidence pieces, none of which a written link changes, so the requests are\n    42\t  the same (a circle correction, if any, would be new). The readers are then known before anything is bought: draw 1 and draw 2, v2,\n    43\t  v9, v16, v17, v21, v35; draw 3, v9, v16, v17, v21. Each control can retire exactly its paired draw's readers from each reader's first\n    44\t  link.\n    45\t- Priced from old-2's stored judgements at published rates: the readers' judgements from their links on cost about $1.0 per sequence\n    46\t  (v2 $0.26, v9 $0.30, v16 $0.15, v17 $0.15, v21 $0.13, v35 $0.05), plus the extra days a changed read question queues its reader\n    47\t  (estimate +30%); three linked and three controls about $7. An estimate, not a ceiling.\n    48\t- **The open question before buying judgements** (for the council, then Alex): measure the current wording as it is, with its\n    49\t  whole-to-part links and one flipping pair disclosed, or first settle the direction of a part against its whole in the criterion,\n    50\t  which changes what the system does (a new arm, probed on these 105 pairs at cents, then Alex).\n     1\t# Claude's own read of the census before Codex round 17 (written before reading codex-r17.md)\n     2\t\n     3\t- The gate passed as registered and is scored as written: no wrong link in 114 W decisions; the known positive right 3 of 3, fragile.\n     4\t- The O links are not errors by the criterion, but they show the class the design named: part-to-whole and whole-to-part both occur,\n     5\t  and v21–v9 flips. In production only one draw happens, so a reader's links depend on a near coin flip for 4 of the 8 pairs.\n     6\t- My lean: measure the current wording as built (three linked sequences taking their links from the census draws, three paired\n     7\t  controls), with the direction class disclosed. Reasons: the paid run answers Alex's question about the version that exists; the\n     8\t  whole-to-part links that occur (growth reading Data Center and CPU, all credit support reading AI-cloud credit support) give the\n     9\t  reader real figures and no W pair was linked; a criterion change is a new arm with its own probe and Alex's choice, and the paid\n    10\t  run's result tells whether linking helps at all before that refinement is worth buying.\n    11\t- Against my lean: if the benefit comes only from part-to-whole links (the whole's market figure reaching the part), a run whose\n    12\t  links point both ways measures a mixture; and the known positive's fragility means the product would miss that link on some days.\n    13\t  A cents probe of a sharpened criterion on the same 105 pairs would settle whether the direction can be fixed before buying ~$7.\n    14\t- Paid design points still open from round 13: paired controls (now exact: each control retires its paired draw's readers from each\n    15\t  reader's first link), the reading rule (part-whole contradiction on matching scope and period; self-made reference traced to an\n    16\t  outside statement; harm), pass/fail/inconclusive defined, the halving rule checked control against control.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
