{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,56p' ./census-result.md; ls -li CENSUS-RESULT.md census-result.md; nl -ba ../../../poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/ledger.json; for i in 1 2 3; do nl -ba ../../../poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/census-\"'$i/draw.json; done; rg -n -A 15 '\"'\"'^## D70[123]'\"' ../../DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"# The census of link decisions over the window: gate PASS by the registered rule; direction unsettled (D700, D701; 2026-11-21)\n\nRun: `poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/` (three draws, each counted: complete, both July seq-148 answers reused, equal to old-2 with no\nlink row; one ledger at Alex's $0.10: settled $0.0266 at the ledger's rule of three times each reported input, 52 attempts, nothing\nrefused or overrun). Scored by `read_census.py` against `expected-links.json` (written before any census answer; R 1, W 38, O 66):\n`census-result.md`.\n\n## By the registered rule\n- **Known positive (v9 Data Center FY2027 reads v14 total revenue FY2027, together):** right in 3 of 3 draws; margins 0.05, 0.09,\n  0.03 (the July samples, fragile).\n- **W pairs (38, the shown material names no connection):** no link in any draw. Wrong links: 0.\n- **Gate: PASS.**\n\n## The O pairs that were linked (reported, not scored)\n\n| seq | pair | draw 1 | draw 2 | draw 3 | reading |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 8 | v2 (all credit support, guarantees, backstops) – v1 (AI-cloud credit support) | v2 reads v1, 0.58 | v2 reads v1, 0.51 | no link (0.48) | a whole reads its part; 2 of 3 |\n| 265 | v16 (total CPU FY2027) – v14 (total revenue FY2027) | v16 reads v14, 0.82 | 0.82 | 0.83 | a part reads its whole; stable |\n| 321 | v17 (total revenue growth FY2028) – v16 (total CPU FY2027) | v17 reads v16, 0.50 | 0.50 | 0.55 | a company-wide figure reads a part of the year before; at the line |\n| 534 | v21 (total revenue growth FY2027) – v16 (total CPU FY2027) | v21 reads v16, 0.73 | 0.72 | 0.76 | a whole reads its part; stable |\n| 534 | v21 – v9 (Data Center FY2027) | v21 reads v9, 0.53 | **v9 reads v21**, 0.52 | v21 reads v9, 0.60 | the direction flips between draws |\n| 1238 | v35 (total revenue FY2028) – v14 (total revenue FY2027) | v35 reads v14, 0.52 | 0.54 | no link (0.44) | another period of the same quantity; 2 of 3 |\n| 1238 | v35 – v9 | no link | v35 reads v9, 0.50 | no link | 1 of 3 |\n\nEvery link written carried the sign together. Links per draw: 7, 8, 5.\n\n## What it shows\n- **No link between unrelated questions.** Across 3 × 38 W decisions, Jev never linked a financing amount to a revenue or margin\n  question, or two financing amounts of different kinds.\n- **The direction of a part against its whole is not settled by the criterion.** The same version reads part-to-whole (v9 → v14,\n  v16 → v14) and whole-to-part (v2 → v1, v21 → v16, v21 → v9), and one pair flips between draws (v21–v9). This is the class §3 named\n  (\"abstract\": the criterion's two clauses admit both directions), now counted on the whole window: of the 8 pairs linked in some draw,\n  4 take the same direction in 3 of 3 draws (v9 → v14, v16 → v14, v17 → v16, v21 → v16), 3 are linked in only 1 or 2 draws, and 1\n  flips direction.\n- **Fragile decisions:** 6 of the linked or required decisions sit within 0.10 of the next class (v9 → v14 in all three; v17 → v16 in\n  two; v21–v9 in one).\n\n## What it means for the paid run\n- A linked sequence of the paid run can take its link answers from its paired census draw: a link request depends on the candidate's\n  state and the shown question's card, ladder and first two evidence pieces, none of which a written link changes, so the requests are\n  the same (a circle correction, if any, would be new). The readers are then known before anything is bought: draw 1 and draw 2, v2,\n  v9, v16, v17, v21, v35; draw 3, v9, v16, v17, v21. Each control can retire exactly its paired draw's readers from each reader's first\n  link.\n- Priced from old-2's stored judgements at published rates: the readers' judgements from their links on cost about $1.0 per sequence\n  (v2 $0.26, v9 $0.30, v16 $0.15, v17 $0.15, v21 $0.13, v35 $0.05), plus the extra days a changed read question queues its reader\n  (estimate +30%); three linked and three controls about $7. An estimate, not a ceiling.\n- **The open question before buying judgements** (for the council, then Alex): measure the current wording as it is, with its\n  whole-to-part links and one flipping pair disclosed, or first settle the direction of a part against its whole in the criterion,\n  which changes what the system does (a new arm, probed on these 105 pairs at cents, then Alex).\n241030388 -rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  4288 Nov 21 03:24 CENSUS-RESULT.md\n241030388 -rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  4288 Nov 21 03:24 census-result.md\n     1\t{\n     2\t \"ceiling\": 0.1,\n     3\t \"spent\": 0.026553870000000004,\n     4\t \"reserved\": 0.0,\n     5\t \"overrun\": false,\n     6\t \"refused\": 0,\n     7\t \"attempts\": 52,\n     8\t \"stopped\": false,\n     9\t \"stop_reason\": null,\n    10\t \"launchers\": {}\n    11\t}     1\t{\n     2\t \"draw\": \"1\",\n     3\t \"transport\": \"paid\",\n     4\t \"counted\": true,\n     5\t \"complete\": true,\n     6\t \"problems\": [],\n     7\t \"equal to old-2\": true,\n     8\t \"july samples reused\": [\n     9\t  \"6dcb76643aea\",\n    10\t  \"d118a387e986\"\n    11\t ],\n    12\t \"ledger\": {\n    13\t  \"ceiling\": 0.1,\n    14\t  \"spent\": 0.00897372,\n    15\t  \"reserved\": 0.0,\n    16\t  \"overrun\": false,\n    17\t  \"refused\": 0,\n    18\t  \"attempts\": 18,\n    19\t  \"stopped\": false,\n    20\t  \"stop_reason\": null,\n    21\t  \"launchers\": {\n    22\t   \"census-1\": \"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/census-1.launcher.lock\"\n    23\t  }\n    24\t }\n    25\t}     1\t{\n     2\t \"draw\": \"2\",\n     3\t \"transport\": \"paid\",\n     4\t \"counted\": true,\n     5\t \"complete\": true,\n     6\t \"problems\": [],\n     7\t \"equal to old-2\": true,\n     8\t \"july samples reused\": [\n     9\t  \"6dcb76643aea\",\n    10\t  \"d118a387e986\"\n    11\t ],\n    12\t \"ledger\": {\n    13\t  \"ceiling\": 0.1,\n    14\t  \"spent\": 0.017947440000000002,\n    15\t  \"reserved\": 0.0,\n    16\t  \"overrun\": false,\n    17\t  \"refused\": 0,\n    18\t  \"attempts\": 36,\n    19\t  \"stopped\": false,\n    20\t  \"stop_reason\": null,\n    21\t  \"launchers\": {\n    22\t   \"census-2\": \"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/census-2.launcher.lock\"\n    23\t  }\n    24\t }\n    25\t}     1\t{\n     2\t \"draw\": \"3\",\n     3\t \"transport\": \"paid\",\n     4\t \"counted\": true,\n     5\t \"complete\": true,\n     6\t \"problems\": [],\n     7\t \"equal to old-2\": true,\n     8\t \"july samples reused\": [\n     9\t  \"6dcb76643aea\",\n    10\t  \"d118a387e986\"\n    11\t ],\n    12\t \"ledger\": {\n    13\t  \"ceiling\": 0.1,\n    14\t  \"spent\": 0.026553870000000004,\n    15\t  \"reserved\": 0.0,\n    16\t  \"overrun\": false,\n    17\t  \"refused\": 0,\n    18\t  \"attempts\": 52,\n    19\t  \"stopped\": false,\n    20\t  \"stop_reason\": null,\n    21\t  \"launchers\": {\n    22\t   \"census-3\": \"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/census-3.launcher.lock\"\n    23\t  }\n    24\t }\n    25\t}10525:## D701 · 2026-11-21 · Council R passes the census harness (rounds 13–16); the census of link decisions is sent under D700\n10526-\n10527-- **The council** (`docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/`, Codex thread `01a1fcdb…`): round 13 NOT READY (no known positive in\n10528-  the gate, July samples not reused, no completeness proof, launcher and ceiling gaps, preflight), round 14 NOT READY (the scorer could\n10529-  pass with no draws and ignored the sign; the registration ruled out links the criterion permits; preflight covered only July),\n10530-  round 15 NOT READY (a dry draw could be scored; the July reuse could fall through to a purchase; three W pairs too strong), round 16\n10531-  READY FOR THE CENSUS SEND. Every finding was taken; each is answered in DESIGN.md §1 and §3.\n10532-- **The $0 proof:** poc-v119 with every link answered \"neither\" equals old-2 over the whole window (1,884 articles, nine projections);\n10533-  14 openings, 105 eligible pairs; the census pass with every pair answered \"reads\" and no link written equals old-2 (105 proposed,\n10534-  0 written), its mutant with links written stops on 07-01; the July answers reused at seq 148 and refused when not pinned; the\n10535-  completeness check and the scorer each catch their mutants; full-window preflight recorded; the registered reading of the 105 pairs\n10536-  (R 1: v9 reads v14, together; W 38; O 66) written before any census answer.\n10537-- **Sent:** `window_test.py census`, draws 1, 2, 3 one after another into `poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/`, one ledger at Alex's\n10538-  $0.10 (D700).\n10539-- **Also recorded:** the July link's direction margins (0.05, 0.09, 0.03; JULY-RESULT.md, added section).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/writing.py | sed -n '112,160p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '40,53p;145,195p;270,358p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py | sed -n '55,69p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/jev.py | sed -n '81,105p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/writing.py | sed -n '112,160p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '40,53p;145,195p;270,358p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py | sed -n '55,69p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/jev.py | sed -n '81,105p'\"","aggregated_output":"   112\t\n   113\tdef write(conn, universe, seq, item, handover, checked, second_pass, *, proposed_links=None):\n   114\t    \"\"\"Write atomically within the caller's transaction; the caller commits the completion marker with it. proposed_links: the reading\n   115\t    links the link step chose (views/links.py, D694), written after the new views exist; None writes none.\"\"\"\n   116\t    if not conn.in_transaction:\n   117\t        conn.execute('begin immediate')\n   118\t    conn.execute('savepoint view_write')\n   119\t    try:\n   120\t        store.ensure_writable_columns(conn)\n   121\t        result = _write(conn, universe, seq, item, handover, checked, second_pass)\n   122\t        if proposed_links:\n   123\t            result.links = _write_links(conn, seq, proposed_links, result)\n   124\t    except Exception:\n   125\t        conn.execute('rollback to view_write')\n   126\t        conn.execute('release view_write')\n   127\t        raise\n   128\t    conn.execute('release view_write')\n   129\t    return result\n   130\t\n   131\t\n   132\tdef _write_links(conn, seq, proposed_links, written):\n   133\t    \"\"\"D694, D695 (design §4): each proposed link resolved to stored ids, re-checked against the ledger as it stands inside this write\n   134\t    (both ends open, no circle, no other label on the same pair), labelled from the stored rungs, written with kind 'reads'. An existing\n   135\t    question that gains a link is judged in the day's round. Any mismatch refuses the whole write.\"\"\"\n   136\t    from . import links as _links\n   137\t    committed = []\n   138\t    for link in proposed_links:\n   139\t        reader, read = (written.new_views.get(link[end], link[end]) for end in ('reader', 'read'))\n   140\t        for end in (reader, read):\n   141\t            if not store.view(conn, end):\n   142\t                raise WriteConflict(f'link {link[\"reader\"]} -> {link[\"read\"]}: {end} was not opened')\n   143\t            if not store.is_open(conn, end):\n   144\t                raise WriteConflict(f'link {reader} -> {read}: {end} is closed')\n   145\t        label = _links.label_for(store.rungs_of(conn, reader), store.rungs_of(conn, read), link['sign'])\n   146\t        if label is None:\n   147\t            raise WriteConflict(f'link {reader} -> {read}: no label can be computed from the stored rungs')\n   148\t        existing = {r['direction'] for r in conn.execute('select direction from dependencies where view_id=? and depends_on=?', (reader, read))}\n   149\t        if existing and existing != {label}:\n   150\t            raise WriteConflict(f'link {reader} -> {read}: the pair already carries another label {sorted(existing)}')\n   151\t        if existing:\n   152\t            continue\n   153\t        if store.would_cycle(conn, reader, read):\n   154\t            raise WriteConflict(f'link {reader} -> {read}: would close a circle')\n   155\t        store.insert(conn, 'dependencies', view_id=reader, depends_on=read, wait_chain_view_id='', wait_year='', direction=label, seq=seq, kind=_links.KIND)\n   156\t        if reader not in written.new_views.values():\n   157\t            written.changed_views.add(reader)\n   158\t        committed.append({'reader': reader, 'read': read, 'label': label, 'sign': link['sign'], 'direction': link['direction']})\n   159\t    return committed\n   160\t\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\tdef evidence_in_view(conn, view_id):\n    43\t    \"\"\"(the pieces a judgement of this thesis reads, how many pieces in force are not shown): the arrivals (linked after the\n    44\t    READINGS-th most recent judgement, or all when there are fewer) and the basis (cited by one of the last BASIS judgements),\n    45\t    both among the evidence in force.\"\"\"\n    46\t    in_force = store.evidence_in_force(conn, view_id)\n    47\t    recent = store.recent_judgements(conn, view_id, BASIS)\n    48\t    arrivals_after = recent[READINGS - 1]['seq'] if len(recent) >= READINGS else -1\n    49\t    basis = {evidence_id for j in recent for evidence_id in j['cites']}\n    50\t    linked_at = {r['evidence_id']: r['seq'] for r in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=?', (view_id,))}\n    51\t    shown = [p for p in in_force if linked_at.get(p['evidence_id'], -1) > arrivals_after or p['evidence_id'] in basis]\n    52\t    return shown, len(in_force) - len(shown)\n    53\t\n   145\t    for p in pieces:\n   146\t        src = p['sources'][0] if p['sources'] else {}\n   147\t        lines.append(f'- {p[\"evidence_id\"]} [{p[\"tier\"]}; {p[\"speaker\"]}; original source {p[\"original_who\"]} {p[\"original_day\"]}; from {src.get(\"input_id\")} {src.get(\"publication_day\")}] {p[\"one_line\"]}\\n    Quote: {p[\"quote\"][:400]}')\n   148\t        if p.get('replaced'):\n   149\t            lines.append(f'    It replaces {p[\"replaced\"][\"evidence_id\"]} ({p[\"replaced\"][\"original_day\"]}): {p[\"replaced\"][\"one_line\"]}')\n   150\t        if p.get('same_as'):\n   151\t            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as {\", \".join(p[\"same_as\"])}; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.')\n   152\t        if p.get('revises'):\n   153\t            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of {p[\"revises\"][\"evidence_id\"]} ({p[\"revises\"][\"original_day\"]}); both are in force: {p[\"revises\"][\"one_line\"]}')\n   154\t    if deps:\n   155\t        lines.append('\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]')\n   156\t        for d in deps:\n   157\t            target = d['resolved_to']\n   158\t            if not target:\n   159\t                lines.append(f'- the {d[\"wait_year\"]} thesis on chain {d[\"wait_chain_view_id\"]}: not yet created ({d[\"direction\"]})')\n   160\t                continue\n   161\t            tv = store.view(conn, target)\n   162\t            state = store.current_state(conn, target)\n   163\t            flag = 'historical only' if d['resolution'] == 'history_only' else ('closed' if not store.is_open(conn, target) else 'open')\n   164\t            rung_label = store.rungs_of(conn, target)[state['rung'] - 1]['label'] if state else 'not judged yet'\n   165\t            if full_dependencies:\n   166\t                lines.extend(_dependency_lines_full(conn, target, d, state, rung_label, tv, flag))\n   167\t                continue\n   168\t            lines.append(f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"] if state else \"-\"} {rung_label}; reasons: {(state or {}).get(\"reasons\", \"\")[:600]}')\n   169\t    if themes:\n   170\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Themes in force, {len(themes)}]')\n   171\t        for theme in themes:\n   172\t            tv, state = theme['view'], theme['state']\n   173\t            mark = f'; {UPDATED_MARK}' if theme['updated'] else ''\n   174\t            lines.append(f'- {theme[\"view_id\"]} ({tv[\"object_id\"]}, due {tv[\"due_day\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"]} {theme[\"rung_label\"]}; '\n   175\t                         f'judged {state[\"publication_day\"]}{mark}; reasons: {(state[\"reasons\"] or \"\")[:THEME_REASONS_CHARS]}')\n   176\t    if last:\n   177\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung {last[\"rung\"]}; reasons: {last[\"reasons\"][:800]}')\n   178\t    else:\n   179\t        lines.append('\\n[Previous conclusion] none: this is the first judgement, so changed must be true.')\n   180\t    lines.append('\\nAnswer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; '\n   181\t                 + ('cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above' if deps else 'cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis')\n   182\t                 + ('; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views' if themes else '') + '.')\n   183\t    return lines\n   184\t\n   185\t\n   186\tdef build_prompt(conn, view_id, prompt_version):\n   187\t    require_supported(prompt_version)\n   188\t    v = store.view(conn, view_id)\n   189\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\n   190\t    pieces, hidden = evidence_in_view(conn, view_id)\n   191\t    deps = store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id)\n   192\t    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n   193\t    lines = _lines_english(conn, view_id, v, rungs, pieces, deps, last, themes_in_force(conn, view_id), hidden=hidden,\n   194\t                           full_dependencies=prompt_version in FULL_DEPENDENCY_BLOCK)\n   195\t    with open(config.prompt_path(prompt_version + '.txt'), encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n   270\t\n   271\tdef upstream(conn, view_id):\n   272\t    \"\"\"Every view this one depends on, directly or through its dependencies.\"\"\"\n   273\t    seen, stack = set(), [view_id]\n   274\t    while stack:\n   275\t        for dep in store.dependencies_of(conn, stack.pop()):\n   276\t            target = dep['resolved_to']\n   277\t            if target and target not in seen:\n   278\t                seen.add(target)\n   279\t                stack.append(target)\n   280\t    return seen\n   281\t\n   282\t\n   283\tdef open_asset_views(conn):\n   284\t    return [v for v in store.open_views(conn) if store.view(conn, v)['object_kind'] != 'theme']\n   285\t\n   286\t\n   287\tdef queued_by_change(conn, view_id):\n   288\t    \"\"\"What a changed conclusion of this view queues: its dependants and, for a theme thesis, every open asset thesis. The one rule,\n   289\t    read for a live judgement and for the judgements a resumed round finds committed.\"\"\"\n   290\t    queued = store.dependants_of(conn, view_id)\n   291\t    if store.view(conn, view_id)['object_kind'] == 'theme':\n   292\t        queued = queued + open_asset_views(conn)\n   293\t    return queued\n   294\t\n   295\t\n   296\tdef queued_by_ledger(conn, seq):\n   297\t    \"\"\"What the judgements already committed at this sequence number queued; a fresh round finds nothing here, a resumed round\n   298\t    finds what the interrupted one had queued in memory.\"\"\"\n   299\t    queued = []\n   300\t    for row in conn.execute('select view_id from judgements where seq=? and changed=1 order by judgement_id', (seq,)):\n   301\t        queued.extend(queued_by_change(conn, row['view_id']))\n   302\t    return queued\n   303\t\n   304\t\n   305\tdef round_of_judgements(archive, cfg, conn, changed_views, seq, item, *, transport=None):\n   306\t    \"\"\"Judge the open views in changed_views, dependencies first; a changed conclusion queues open dependants.\n   307\t\n   308\t    Views that do not depend on each other are judged at the same time: each level of the dependency order is sent\n   309\t    to the model concurrently (the prompts are built and the answers checked and written in this thread, so the\n   310\t    database connection never crosses threads). A view waits while anything upstream of it is still pending, so a\n   311\t    dependant always reads this round's conclusion of its dependency. A view with no evidence in force stays\n   312\t    unjudged (D59), and a view already judged at this sequence number (a resumed round) is not judged twice.\n   313\t\n   314\t    Among the views ready to be judged, theme theses go first, so an asset thesis reads this round's theme conclusions; a theme judgement that says changed queues every open asset thesis with\n   315\t    evidence in force. The starting queue adds what the ledger says earlier commits at this sequence number queued.\"\"\"\n   316\t    import concurrent.futures\n   317\t\n   318\t    version = cfg.rejudging.prompt_version\n   319\t    schema = schema_for(version)\n   320\t\n   321\t    def eligible(view_id):\n   322\t        return store.is_open(conn, view_id) and not store.has_judgement(conn, view_id, seq) and bool(store.evidence_in_force(conn, view_id))\n   323\t\n   324\t    def is_theme(view_id):\n   325\t        return store.view(conn, view_id)['object_kind'] == 'theme'\n   326\t\n   327\t    pending = [v for v in topological(conn, list(changed_views) + queued_by_ledger(conn, seq)) if eligible(v)]\n   328\t    done, results = set(), []\n   329\t    while pending:\n   330\t        ready = [v for v in pending if upstream(conn, v).isdisjoint(set(pending) - {v})] or pending[:1]\n   331\t        level = [v for v in ready if is_theme(v)] or ready\n   332\t        prompts = {v: build_prompt(conn, v, version) for v in level}\n   333\t\n   334\t        def ask(view_id, note=''):\n   335\t            system, user = prompts[view_id]\n   336\t            return model.call(archive, cfg, cfg.rejudging, system, user + note, schema, 'judgement', 'judge', transport=transport)\n   337\t\n   338\t        with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=JUDGE_WORKERS) as pool_:\n   339\t            answers = dict(zip(level, pool_.map(ask, level)))\n   340\t        for view_id in level:\n   341\t            answer = answers[view_id]\n   342\t            errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data, prompts[view_id][1])\n   343\t            if errors:\n   344\t                archive.retire(answer.call_id)                 # a refused answer never answers the same request again (a resume re-samples)\n   345\t                answer = ask(view_id, retry_note(errors))\n   346\t                errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data, prompts[view_id][1])\n   347\t                if errors:\n   348\t                    archive.retire(answer.call_id)\n   349\t                    raise JudgementRefused(f'{view_id}: ' + '; '.join(errors))\n   350\t            result = _record(conn, cfg, view_id, seq, item, answer)\n   351\t            done.add(view_id)\n   352\t            results.append(result)\n   353\t            if result['changed']:\n   354\t                for dependant in queued_by_change(conn, view_id):\n   355\t                    if dependant not in done and dependant not in pending and eligible(dependant):\n   356\t                        pending.append(dependant)\n   357\t        pending = [v for v in topological(conn, pending) if v not in done and eligible(v)]\n   358\t    return results\n    55\t\n    56\tdef candidate_state(c, evidence):\n    57\t    rungs = ' / '.join(f'{r[\"label\"]}: {r[\"condition\"]}' for r in c['rungs'])\n    58\t    fields = ', '.join(f'{f}={c[f]}' for f in ('measure', 'scope', 'period_start', 'period_end', 'basis', 'unit', 'event_type') if c.get(f) not in (None, '', 'n/a'))\n    59\t    own = ' | '.join(f'[{e[\"speaker\"]} {e[\"original_day\"]}] {e[\"quote\"][:400]}' for e in evidence if e['id'] in c.get('evidence_ids', []))[:1600]\n    60\t    return (f'CANDIDATE ({c[\"kind\"]}, object {c[\"object\"]}, focus \"{c[\"looks_at\"]}\", {c[\"year\"]}, due {c[\"due_day\"]}): {c[\"question\"]}\\n'\n    61\t            f'Key: {fields}\\nLadder: {rungs}\\nIts evidence: {own}')\n    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\tdef thesis_text(conn, view_id):\n    65\t    \"\"\"The thesis as the judge should see it: the card and the quotes that define it (its first two pieces in force).\"\"\"\n    66\t    pieces = store.evidence_in_force(conn, view_id)[:2]\n    67\t    quotes = ''.join(f'\\n    Evidence: [{p[\"speaker\"]} {p[\"original_day\"]}] {p[\"quote\"][:400]}' for p in pieces)\n    68\t    return matching.describe_view(conn, view_id, english=True) + quotes\n    69\t\n    81\t\n    82\tdef request_for(setting, state, questions):\n    83\t    \"\"\"The complete Jev request used both for dispatch and in-flight identity.\"\"\"\n    84\t    return {'model': setting.model, 'state': state, 'questions': questions}\n    85\t\n    86\t\n    87\tdef ask(archive, cfg, setting, state, questions, purpose, *, transport=None):\n    88\t    \"\"\"One Jev request, archived; returns model.Answer whose data is the `answers` map.\"\"\"\n    89\t    request = request_for(setting, state, questions)\n    90\t    request_json, sha = model.request_identity(request)\n    91\t    prompt_chars = len(request_json)\n    92\t    hit = archive.lookup(sha)\n    93\t    if hit:\n    94\t        call_id, answer_json, _, input_tokens, output_tokens = hit\n    95\t        return model.Answer(json.loads(answer_json), call_id, sha, True, prompt_chars, input_tokens or 0, output_tokens or 0, 0.0)\n    96\t    started = time.time()\n    97\t    response = (transport or globals()['transport'])(request)\n    98\t    seconds = round(time.time() - started, 2)\n    99\t    answers = response.get('answers') if isinstance(response, dict) else None\n   100\t    problems = validate(answers, questions)\n   101\t    usage = response.get('usage') or {} if isinstance(response, dict) else {}\n   102\t    input_tokens, output_tokens = int(usage.get('input_tokens') or 0), int(usage.get('output_tokens') or 0)\n   103\t    price_in, _ = model.PRICES.get(setting.model, (0.0, 0.0))\n   104\t    cost = round(input_tokens / 1e6 * price_in, 6)\n   105\t    call_id = archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
