tions\\\"])==c[\\\"questions\\\"] and purpose==\\\"match\\\"\n   if sha in juli:\n    assert juli[sha]==resp\n    used.append(sha[:12])\n   for key,v in ans.items():\n    target=key.split(\\\"__\\\")[1]\n    stage=c[\\\"stage\\\"]\n    assert parsed[(seq,target)][stage]==v[\\\"choice\\\"] and parsed[(seq,target)][\\\"p\\\" if stage==\\\"reads\\\" else \\\"sp\\\"]==v[\\\"probabilities\\\"]\n    if stage==\\\"reads\\\" and (seq,target) in watches and (seq,target) not in shown:\n     shown.add((seq,target))\n     print(\\\"PAIR\\\",seq,target,sha[:12])\n     print(req[\\\"state\\\"].splitlines()[0],req[\\\"state\\\"].splitlines()[-1])\n     print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(line for idx,line in enumerate(req[\\\"questions\\\"][key][\\\"instructions\\\"].splitlines()) if idx==1 or line.lstrip().startswith(\\\"Evidence:\\\")))\n  proposed=[]\n  for link in item[\\\"proposed\\\"]:\n   l=dict(link)\n   new=reg[\\\"{}:{}\\\".format(seq,l[\\\"thesis\\\"])][\\\"new\\\"]\n   for end in (\\\"reader\\\",\\\"read\\\"):\n    if l[end]==l[\\\"candidate\\\"]: l[end]=new\n   proposed.append(l)\n  assert not links.circles(g,proposed)\n  for l in proposed:\n   edges.append((seq,l[\\\"reader\\\"],l[\\\"read\\\"],l[\\\"sign\\\"]))\n   store.insert(g,\\\"dependencies\\\",view_id=l[\\\"reader\\\"],depends_on=l[\\\"read\\\"],kind=\\\"reads\\\",seq=seq)\n print(\\\"COUNTS\\\",dict(counts),\\\"reused\\\",used,\\\"calls paid\\\",sum(counts.values())-len(used),\\\"edges\\\",edges)\n print(\\\"score\\\",r.score([(str(i),parsed)],reg)[1])'\"","aggregated_output":"DRAW 1 complete (True, []) unmet refusals [] stored links 0\nPAIR 8 v1 08909f1721dd\nCANDIDATE (asset, object NVDA, focus \"NVIDIA's credit support and capacity backstop obligations to customers and cloud providers\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): At NVIDIA's FY2027 annual report, how much will its commitments for customer and cloud-provider credit support, guarantees, and capacity backstops reach? Its evidence: [moomoo.com 2026-07-01] On July 1, according to the technology news outlet The Information, NVIDIA is providing financial guarantees to young cloud service providers that lease or rent its GPUs—if these companies fail to secure enough AI developers to rent their computing capacity, NVIDIA will repurchase their unsold GPU capacity at a pre-agreed price. | [moomoo.com 2026-07-01] On July 1, NVIDIA published a statement on its official website announcing a new business model that combines revenue sharing with credit support, enabling AI cloud providers to procure NVIDIA infrastructure without bearing the full upfront capital expenditure, and allowing them to offer computing services to downstream AI-native enterprises, model developers, and corporate clients. | [moomoo.com ] According to a regulatory filing submitted by NVIDIA in May of this year (covering the quarter ended in April), NVIDIA subsequently added another $3.5 billion to guarantee customer data center leases in exchange for rights to purchase their shares.\nv1 (open, NVDA, asset, focus \"The amount of NVIDIA's credit-support obligations under the AI-cloud revenue-sharing and credit-support model.\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much credit support will NVIDIA have committed under its AI-cloud model by the publication of its FY2027 annual report?\n    Evidence: [NVIDIA Corporation 2026-07-01] This new model enables AI clouds to procure NVIDIA infrastructure for AI-native, enterprise and ISV customers through economic alignment with a revenue-sharing and credit-support model. Through the partnership, AI clouds will sell NVIDIA-powered cloud services, with NVIDIA earning both standard product revenue and a share of the cloud revenue on the supported capacity. This structure accelerates a\nPAIR 148 v9 6dcb76643aea\nCANDIDATE (asset, object NVDA, focus \"NVIDIA FY2027 total revenue\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027? Its evidence: [Jeran Wittenstein, citing data compiled by Bloomberg ] The chipmaker is projected to deliver $228 billion in profits on sales of $393 billion in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31. That would represent an expansion of 90% and 82%, respectively, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\nv9 (open, NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA FY2027 Data Center segment revenue\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n    Evidence: [tradingview.com ] During the first quarter of fiscal 2027, the Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenues, accounting for 92% of total sales. Revenues from the segment surged 92% year over year and grew 21% sequentially, driven by the rapid ramp-up of Blackwell 300 systems and robust networking demand.\n    Evidence: [NVIDIA 2026-07-07] NVIDIA is collaborating with Nokia to deliver AI-RAN platforms integrated with Nokia anyRAN software for AI-native 5G-Advanced networks ready for 6G evolution.\nPAIR 265 v14 1c43ea12177c\nCANDIDATE (asset, object NVDA, focus \"NVIDIA total CPU revenue in FY2027\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much total CPU revenue will NVIDIA generate in FY2027? Its evidence: [trefis.com, quoting NVIDIA management ] opens a brand new $200 billion TAM for NVIDIA, a market we have never addressed before. | [trefis.com, quoting NVIDIA management ] visibility to nearly $20 billion in total CPU revenue this year.\nv14 (open, NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA FY2027 total revenue\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n    Evidence: [Jeran Wittenstein, citing data compiled by Bloomberg ] The chipmaker is projected to deliver $228 billion in profits on sales of $393 billion in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31. That would represent an expansion of 90% and 82%, respectively, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\n    Evidence: [es.tradingview.com ] The bank noted that AI laboratories now account for roughly 20% of Nvidia’s demand, highlighting how enterprise AI adoption is expanding beyond hyperscale cloud providers.\nPAIR 321 v16 3225952a7a4f\nCANDIDATE (asset, object NVDA, focus \"NVIDIA FY2028 total revenue growth\", FY2028, due 2028-02-28): How much will NVIDIA's total revenue grow in FY2028? Its evidence: [fool.com (analyst) ] they also predict growth slowing to a 41% revenue increase for fiscal 2028.\nv16 (open, NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA total CPU revenue in FY2027\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much total CPU revenue will NVIDIA generate in FY2027?\n    Evidence: [trefis.com, quoting NVIDIA management ] opens a brand new $200 billion TAM for NVIDIA, a market we have never addressed before.\n    Evidence: [trefis.com, quoting NVIDIA management ] visibility to nearly $20 billion in total CPU revenue this year.\nPAIR 534 v16 c0e793b863d1\nCANDIDATE (asset, object NVDA, focus \"NVIDIA total revenue growth in FY2027\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much will NVIDIA's total revenue grow in FY2027? Its evidence: [Keithen Drury, The Motley Fool ] By the end of fiscal year 2027 (ending August 2027), Wall Street expects an additional 84% growth for Micron, while it estimates only 42% for Nvidia.\nv16 (open, NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA total CPU revenue in FY2027\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much total CPU revenue will NVIDIA generate in FY2027?\n    Evidence: [trefis.com, quoting NVIDIA management ] opens a brand new $200 billion TAM for NVIDIA, a market we have never addressed before.\n    Evidence: [trefis.com, quoting NVIDIA management ] visibility to nearly $20 billion in total CPU revenue this year.\nPAIR 534 v9 c0e793b863d1\nCANDIDATE (asset, object NVDA, focus \"NVIDIA total revenue growth in FY2027\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much will NVIDIA's total revenue grow in FY2027? Its evidence: [Keithen Drury, The Motley Fool ] By the end of fiscal year 2027 (ending August 2027), Wall Street expects an additional 84% growth for Micron, while it estimates only 42% for Nvidia.\nv9 (open, NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA FY2027 Data Center segment revenue\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n    Evidence: [tradingview.com ] During the first quarter of fiscal 2027, the Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenues, accounting for 92% of total sales. Revenues from the segment surged 92% year over year and grew 21% sequentially, driven by the rapid ramp-up of Blackwell 300 systems and robust networking demand.\n    Evidence: [NVIDIA 2026-07-07] NVIDIA is collaborating with Nokia to deliver AI-RAN platforms integrated with Nokia anyRAN software for AI-native 5G-Advanced networks ready for 6G evolution.\nPAIR 1238 v14 66efa39f1070\nCANDIDATE (asset, object NVDA, focus \"How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2028?\", FY2028, due 2028-02-28): How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2028? Its evidence: [fool.com (analyst) ] Analysts see revenue reaching about $390 billion in 2027 and more than $550 billion in 2028, with annual sales growth of roughly 24% to 25%. | [fool.com (analyst), reporting NVIDIA management's outlook ] Management's outlook is even stronger: about 70% growth in fiscal 2028, which could put revenue near $670 billion.\nv14 (open, NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA FY2027 total revenue\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n    Evidence: [Jeran Wittenstein, citing data compiled by Bloomberg ] The chipmaker is projected to deliver $228 billion in profits on sales of $393 billion in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31. That would represent an expansion of 90% and 82%, respectively, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\n    Evidence: [es.tradingview.com ] The bank noted that AI laboratories now account for roughly 20% of Nvidia’s demand, highlighting how enterprise AI adoption is expanding beyond hyperscale cloud providers.\nPAIR 1238 v9 66efa39f1070\nCANDIDATE (asset, object NVDA, focus \"How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2028?\", FY2028, due 2028-02-28): How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2028? Its evidence: [fool.com (analyst) ] Analysts see revenue reaching about $390 billion in 2027 and more than $550 billion in 2028, with annual sales growth of roughly 24% to 25%. | [fool.com (analyst), reporting NVIDIA management's outlook ] Management's outlook is even stronger: about 70% growth in fiscal 2028, which could put revenue near $670 billion.\nv9 (open, NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA FY2027 Data Center segment revenue\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n    Evidence: [tradingview.com ] During the first quarter of fiscal 2027, the Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenues, accounting for 92% of total sales. Revenues from the segment surged 92% year over year and grew 21% sequentially, driven by the rapid ramp-up of Blackwell 300 systems and robust networking demand.\n    Evidence: [NVIDIA 2026-07-07] NVIDIA is collaborating with Nokia to deliver AI-RAN platforms integrated with Nokia anyRAN software for AI-native 5G-Advanced networks ready for 6G evolution.\nCOUNTS {'reads': 14, 'sign': 6} reused ['6dcb76643aea', 'd118a387e986'] calls paid 18 edges [(8, 'v2', 'v1', 'together'), (148, 'v9', 'v14', 'together'), (265, 'v16', 'v14', 'together'), (321, 'v17', 'v16', 'together'), (534, 'v21', 'v16', 'together'), (534, 'v21', 'v9', 'together'), (1238, 'v35', 'v14', 'together')]\nscore {'right': [('1', '148:v9')], 'missed': [], 'wrong': [], 'fragile': [('1', '148:v9', 0.05), ('1', '321:v16', 0.03)], 'gate': True}\nDRAW 2 complete (True, []) unmet refusals [] stored links 0\nCOUNTS {'reads': 14, 'sign': 6} reused ['6dcb76643aea', 'd118a387e986'] calls paid 18 edges [(8, 'v2', 'v1', 'together'), (148, 'v9', 'v14', 'together'), (265, 'v16', 'v14', 'together'), (321, 'v17', 'v16', 'together'), (534, 'v21', 'v16', 'together'), (534, 'v9', 'v21', 'together'), (1238, 'v35', 'v14', 'together'), (1238, 'v35', 'v9', 'together')]\nscore {'right': [('2', '148:v9')], 'missed': [], 'wrong': []